l,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.dev.custom_build [61accf060]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev (61accf060) - macOS 14.5.0 - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Max (Apple7) - Apple M1 Max (10 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe yellow circle of the output button indicates a warning:\r\n\r\n![1](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c30338d5-ed3a-4e7b-ab76-cdb6808fdf60)\r\n\r\nHowever, when the button is pressed it turns pale green:\r\n\r\n![2](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6eec5e5-21df-4fa5-a5ea-05b76c7e85ed)\r\n\r\nIf the icon saturation is set to 2 it gets bright green:\r\n\r\n![3](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27b8d75c-01f5-4df5-a7f3-174e4e6612de)\r\n\r\nThis changes the meaning of the icon to the opposite and can be confusing to users because green means success. Which is why I'm reporting this as an issue\r\n\r\nSame happens in log filter buttons:\r\n\r\n![4](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/866806c3-be0d-478c-823e-91b7dfd736c2)\r\n\r\nButtons with colored icons should have special treatment and never be tinted. Tint only makes sense for monochrome icons\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSet icon saturation to 2. You can also experiment with different accent colors, personally I use a more saturated shade of blue which makes the problem more noticeable\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https